%S A297535 1,5,7,187,381,27047,72989,10085845,33920411,7762776869,31274211423,
%T A297535 10733718804235,50391974346781,24257513141028095,130043317838365621,
%U A297535 83670735493037653765
%N A297535 Number of maximum matchings in the n-Andrásfai graph.
%H A297535 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/AndrasfaiGraph.html">Andrásfai Graph</a>
%H A297535 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Matching.html">Matching</a>
%H A297535 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/MaximumIndependentEdgeSet.html">Maximum Independent Edge Set</a>
%F A297535 a(n) = [t^epsilon_n]P_n(t,t,t), where epsilon_n = (1 + (-1)^n)/2 and P_n(x,y,z) = B*A*(C*B*A)^(n-1) 1, with A = x + d/dz, B = y + d/dx, and C = z + d/dy. The operators act from right to left, before substituting x = y = z = t. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 26 2026
%e A297535 For n = 3, epsilon_3 = 0 and P_3(t,t,t) = t^8 + 12*t^6 + 42*t^4 + 44*t^2 + 7. Hence a(3) = [t^0]P_3(t,t,t) = 7.
%e A297535 For n = 4, epsilon_4 = 1 and P_4(t,t,t) = t^11 + 22*t^9 + 165*t^7 + 506*t^5 + 594*t^3 + 187*t. Hence a(4) = [t^1]P_4(t,t,t) = 187.
%K A297535 nonn,more,changed
%O A297535 1,2
